      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. Problems of Indian Agriculture"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "ktnvakv",
      "content": "• Small land holdings."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "gv3a37o",
      "content": "• Dependence on monsoon."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "y3iqpr7",
      "content": "• Low productivity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wtwxx9c",
      "content": "• Lack of modern technology."
    },
    {
      "id": "op9v0ng",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. Government Initiatives"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Distinction between Kharif, Rabi, and Zaid cropping seasons, including exact sowing and harvesting months and crop categories.",
        "Local names of shifting cultivation: Jhum (North-East India), Kumari (Western Ghats), and Bewar/Dahiya (Madhya Pradesh).",
        "Government initiative slogans and details: PMKSY ('Har Khet Ko Pani' & 'Per Drop More Crop'), Soil Health Card ('Swasth Dharaa, Khet Haraa'), and PM-KISAN (₹6,000 annually in 3 equal instalments).",
        "Establishment year and committee for NABARD (July 12, 1982; B. Sivaraman Committee) and the pioneer of Operation Flood (Dr. Verghese Kurien in 1970)."
      ],
      "id": "d77kwt4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "qq7vp3e",
      "content": "• Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana – crop insurance scheme."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z4tutgt",
      "content": "• Soil Health Card Scheme – improves soil fertility."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c0aowyb",
      "content": "• Pradhan Mantri Krishi Sinchai Yojana – irrigation development."
    },
    {
